{"text": "H-107 State House\nAnnapolis, Maryland 21401-1991\n410-841-3600 - 301-858-3600\n800-492-7122 Ext. 3600\nBill.Ferguson@senate.state.md.us\n\nBritt Fercuson\nPRESIDENT OF THE SENATE\nLegislative District 46\n\nBaltimore City\n\nThe Senate of Maryland\n\nANNAPOLIS, MARYLAND 21401-1991\n\nMEMORANDUM\nTO: Senate of Maryland\nFROM: Bill Ferguson EP ;\nSenate President\nDATE: February 8, 2022\nRE: Return to In-Person Committee Hearings\n\nAs discussed over the last several weeks and noted in the January 5\"\" 2022 Regular Session\nInformation and Protocols, my goal has been to return to in-person committee hearings on\nFebruary 14\" if safe to do so. Based on the marked improvements seen in current COVID-19\nstatistics and data and guidance from public health experts, I believe we can move forward with\nthis plan safely.\n\nBeginning February 14\u2018, standing committee hearings will be in-person and\n\nmembers of the public will have access to the seating in committee rooms. All standing\ncommittee hearings and voting will be live-streamed on the Maryland General Assembly (MGA)\n\nwebsite. The full Senate of Maryland will continue convening in person in the Senate Chamber.\nMasks will still be required in all areas of the Legislative Complex, weekly testing requirements\nwill remain, and seating will be limited in the seating areas of committee rooms.\n\nBelow are guidelines that review the protocols for the Senate of Maryland effective\nFebruary 14\". Please know that I am committed to protecting the health of all members, staff, and\nthe public, and will continue monitoring the situation. As always, thank you for your\nunderstanding and cooperation.\n\nMasking Policy\n\nAll members and staff must continue to wear face masks to gain entrance to any legislative\nbuilding, and consistently in all public spaces regardless of vaccination status. This includes",
